      "writtenOn": "2025-12-02T01:32:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t this be a behavior of OpenLoaded instead of special-casing it here? That is, if a lib was opened using OpenLoaded, then it shouldn\u0027t be closeable, because it\u0027s OpenLoaded is not \"RAII\" (no \"resource acquisition\").\n\nSeems like DynamicLib isn\u0027t quite the right abstraction here and maybe this type of DynamicLib is a class-hierarchy-sibling of that one.",
      "parentUuid": "c7c1519b_dcb376aa",
      "range": {
